      "message": "Hi Aseda,\nfollowing up on the HpdWake issues we talked about earlier this year. After the initial CL which seemed to help with EC wake event logging re-landed, the HpdWake test continued to fail on Brya (https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3615033).\n\nGoing back to this, it looks like there is a bug with how we register the EC_MKBP_EVENT_DP_ALT_MODE_ENTERED source. We declare it in a TCPMv1 only file. Then, when a TCPMv2 EC tries to send this message to the kernel, it fails with a \"HC 0x0067 err 2\" error because mkbp_get_next_event in mkbp_event.c cannot find the source. \n\nCan you take a look at this fix? It just moves the source declaration to a TCPMv1/TCPMv2 common file.",
